WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.305
"Are you ready to sell some T-shirts?"

2
00:00:05.306 --> 00:00:09.858
Ally asked Mateo as they carried boxes onto the soccer field the next day.

3
00:00:09.859 --> 00:00:13.707
They had just picked up the T-shirts from the print shop.

4
00:00:13.708 --> 00:00:16.365
"I sure am," Mateo said.

5
00:00:16.366 --> 00:00:19.910
Ally looked at the field.

6
00:00:19.911 --> 00:00:23.360
"I hope lots of people show up to help out."

7
00:00:23.361 --> 00:00:29.086
"I don't think we have to worry about that." Mateo grinned. "Look at the field!"

8
00:00:29.087 --> 00:00:30.942
Kate and Bethany were there.

9
00:00:30.943 --> 00:00:37.177
And so was Barry, along with everyone from soccer camp.

10
00:00:37.178 --> 00:00:41.504
On the opposite side of the field, Ally saw even more people.

11
00:00:41.505 --> 00:00:47.856
"It looks like those people are already collecting signatures for our petition!" Ally smiled.

12
00:00:47.857 --> 00:00:51.488
"Kate did a great job spreading the word around town.

13
00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:56.666
I'm so happy this many people showed up to save the soccer field."

14
00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:02.076
"Uh, I'm not sure that's why everyone is here," Mateo said.

15
00:01:02.077 --> 00:01:04.679
Ally followed his gaze across the field.

16
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.404
Those people were wearing T-shirts too.

17
00:01:07.405 --> 00:01:11.437
But theirs read People for More Parking.

18
00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:17.663
Ally frowned. "Why would anyone want a parking lot more than a soccer field?"

19
00:01:17.664 --> 00:01:21.738
Then her face lit up. "I'm going to talk to them!

20
00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:28.666
I'll use my Astralian powers to convince them that Sandville needs to keep this soccer field."

21
00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:33.313
Ally hurried over to a man who was collecting signatures for the parking lot.

22
00:01:33.314 --> 00:01:37.113
She asked why he wanted a new parking lot.

23
00:01:37.114 --> 00:01:42.108
"Since more tourists started coming to town, it's become impossible to find a parking spot."

24
00:01:42.109 --> 00:01:46.012
The man scowled. "Customers can't come to our stores.

25
00:01:46.013 --> 00:01:50.643
We can't park to run errands. It's a nightmare!"

26
00:01:50.644 --> 00:01:53.489
"I didn't think of all that," Ally said.

27
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:58.410
"But having a place for people to play soccer is important too."

28
00:01:58.411 --> 00:02:01.426
"You can't have everything, kid," the man said.

29
00:02:01.427 --> 00:02:04.706
"We'll just have to see which side collects more signatures.

30
00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:07.490
But I doubt it will be your side.

31
00:02:07.491 --> 00:02:12.180
We already have more than two hundred signatures from Sandville residents."

32
00:02:12.181 --> 00:02:16.935
Ally gasped. More than two hundred signatures?

33
00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:22.000
"I guess we lost," she thought as she headed back to her friends.

34
00:02:22.001 --> 00:02:27.849
"I thought I'd be able to go home and tell my parents about all the great things I did in Sandville.

35
00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:36.473
But now I'll have to go home and admit I messed things up."

36
00:02:36.474 --> 00:02:39.603
"Ally, what did that man say?" Barry asked.

37
00:02:39.604 --> 00:02:45.832
Ally shook her head. "That we'll have to see which side can collect more signatures.

38
00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:49.401
And they already have over two hundred!"

39
00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:53.817
Julius shrugged. "Then I guess we'd better get to work."

40
00:02:53.818 --> 00:02:58.658
"You think we can get more signatures than they got?" Ally asked.

41
00:02:58.659 --> 00:03:02.520
"We'll never know if we don't try," Julius said.

42
00:03:02.521 --> 00:03:05.341
"Julius is right," Mateo said.

43
00:03:05.342 --> 00:03:11.711
"Let's fan out around town and get as many signatures as we can."

44
00:03:11.712 --> 00:03:15.835
The soccer kids broke up into small groups and headed into town.

45
00:03:15.836 --> 00:03:21.176
Soon the only people left at the field were Ally, Barry, and Julius.

46
00:03:21.177 --> 00:03:23.676
Julius' cheeks turned pink.

47
00:03:23.677 --> 00:03:28.585
"Do you want to go to the UFO Museum with me to collect signatures, Ally?"

48
00:03:28.586 --> 00:03:33.508
Ally wasn't trying to read his mind, but she could sense something strong.

49
00:03:33.509 --> 00:03:36.502
"He likes me," she thought.

50
00:03:36.503 --> 00:03:41.824
"It's the same feeling that Mateo had for Bethany before they'd started dating."

51
00:03:41.825 --> 00:03:45.849
And she liked him back.

52
00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:50.073
"But I'm leaving soon and never coming back," Ally thought.

53
00:03:50.074 --> 00:03:54.243
"I can't explain that, and I don't want to fib again."

54
00:03:54.244 --> 00:04:00.224
"Um," Ally fumbled for words. "I, um, no thanks.

55
00:04:00.225 --> 00:04:05.594
Barry's going to the diner to collect signatures. I think I'll just go there too."

56
00:04:05.595 --> 00:04:11.461
Julius looked hurt. "See you later," he mumbled as he walked away.

57
00:04:11.462 --> 00:04:14.590
"Ugh!" Ally thought in frustration.

58
00:04:14.591 --> 00:04:20.322
"I hurt his feelings again . . . maybe this time I should have told a fib!"

59
00:04:20.323 --> 00:04:24.150
"Are you ready to go collect signatures, Ally?" Barry asked.

60
00:04:24.151 --> 00:04:29.040
"Sure." Ally sighed.

61
00:04:29.041 --> 00:04:37.147
While Ally and Barry collected signatures outside the diner, they talked about the menu for Ally's surprise Holly Days party.

62
00:04:37.148 --> 00:04:40.898
"This is going to be an unusual party," Barry said.

63
00:04:40.899 --> 00:04:44.733
"That's for sure!" Ally laughed.

64
00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:50.130
"Barry! Can you come here, please?" Ray called Barry into the diner.

65
00:04:50.131 --> 00:04:53.896
A few minutes later, Barry was back.

66
00:04:53.897 --> 00:04:56.557
"What was that about?" Ally asked.

67
00:04:56.558 --> 00:04:59.794
"It was about me saving your party."

68
00:04:59.795 --> 00:05:02.111
"Huh? What do you mean?"

69
00:05:02.112 --> 00:05:07.020
Barry grinned proudly. "Ray heard us talking about a surprise party.

70
00:05:07.021 --> 00:05:14.473
He asked me who was throwing one, so I told him someone called to book a party here. Good idea, right?"

71
00:05:14.474 --> 00:05:21.322
"What?" Ally slapped her forehead. "No, Barry! That was a terrible idea!

72
00:05:21.323 --> 00:05:29.194
Now Ray thinks he has to cook and shop for a party that's not real!"

